.TH IAD\-CONTENT\-AREA 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
content_area \- See the module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
content_area(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M>>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBcontent_area\fR: marks the region of the window that is the page's content (the pane beside the sidebar, between the bars), so a \fBPopover\fR opened from inside it stays inside it instead of sliding under the sidebar or a bar.
.PP
The widget changes nothing about layout or drawing. While it collects the overlays of what it wraps, it records its own bounds, and a popover being created there reads them. A popover whose trigger is outside every content area (a header bar button, a sidebar row) simply uses the window. \fBPopoverBounds::Window\fR opts a popover out.
.PP
The library's own panes are already marked (\fBToolbarView\fR's content, the content of \fBNavigationSplitView\fR and \fBOverlaySplitView\fR); wrap your own content pane with \fBcontent_area\fR when you lay a window out yourself.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B content_area(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M>>)
Marks \fBcontent\fR as a content area.
